WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.901
-welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.167
You're here.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.234
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.634
You guys, it's the first day
of spring.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.901
Today.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:14.367
Soon, the weather will jump
from 16 to 64.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.801
It's basically the opposite
of March madness.

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:22.701
Yeah, it's officially spring.
April showers, May flowers.

00:00:22.701 --> 00:00:24.968
By the way, those are two more
porn stars Trump bribed

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:25.968
with hush money.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:29.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.100
April -- April showers.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.601
Everyone is talking about this.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:34.801
Over the weekend, Trump posted
on social media that he expects

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.834
to be arrested
for hush money payments

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.734
to Stormy Daniels.

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:39.767
Trump said...

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.601
First of all, at least
he's finally admitting

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.167
he's the former president.

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:53.300
That's progress.
Progress.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.834
Baby steps.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.133
You've got to give it to him.
It's not often that everyone

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.901
sends out a "save the date"
for their own arrest.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.234
You know what I mean?

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:02.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.567
And I read that Trump is not
excited about being arrested,

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.667
fingerprinted,
or asking for bail.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.501
But he is excited
to get frisked.

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:12.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.934
Yep. Police are going to be
like, "You have the right

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:16.434
to remain silent now,
but also in general.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.601
Just think about it.
Just something to think about."

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.167
You know, if they want Trump's
fingerprints,

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.667
they could have just looked
at the Cheeto dust

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:22.701
on his Diet Coke cans.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:25.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:27.300
And get this, after Trump said
that he expects to be arrested,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.634
he urged his supporters
to stand up for him, writing...

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.734
Yeah, even his supporters
were thinking,

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.067
"Yeah, that really worked out
well for us last time."

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.033
Definitely think about that.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.834
Right now, Facebook, Twitter,
and YouTube are like,

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.601
"Come on, man.
We just gave your accounts back.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:45.901
Please."

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.667
That's right. Trump thinks
he's going to be arrested

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.868
for hush money payments
to Stormy Daniels.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:52.100
Some people may find the
situation a little confusing,

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.300
so let's break it
down in pictures.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.734
Trump said that he's about to be
arrested, and as a result,

00:01:56.734 --> 00:01:58.868
he's absolutely furious.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.501
But this case isn't that simple.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.534
It's not just black and white.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.200
The only reason we know
an arrest is coming

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.334
is because Trump told us.

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:08.901
He leaked it himself.

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:10.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.467
It all started when Trump paid
Stormy Daniels for her silence.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.133
He wanted the story
to disappear.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.567
But it didn't.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.667
And now that Trump's claiming
that all the charges against him

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.033
are totally made up...

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.501
...he's hoping that prosecutors

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:26.234
might let the whole thing slide.

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:28.400
But in the end, they're
indicting him, which, for Trump,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.067
is a huge,
crushing disappointment.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.267
Thank you.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.834
The photos help move it along.

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.667
♪♪

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.567
Meanwhile, Mike Pence said that
the indictment of Trump

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:44.834
is not what
the American people want to see.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.300
Yeah, pretty strong words.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.601
But when someone asked
Mike Pence,

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.701
"What do the American people
want to see?"

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:50.834
He said this.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.367
-♪ I'm a scat man ♪

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:55.367
[ Scatting ]

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:59.801
♪♪

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.501
-What?
-What?

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.267
-I'm not sure he knows
what people want

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.901
to and want to not see.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.434
Yeah, Trump might be indicted
and arrested tomorrow.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.901
He could be
in a lot of legal trouble.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.200
But luckily for him,
he's an expert on the law.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.133
I mean, look at the definitions
that he has

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:14.634
for some common legal terms.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:17.167
First up, when asked what
habeas corpus means,

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.167
Trump said...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.300
Next up, for bail, he said...

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.501
When asked what subpoena is,
he said...

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:35.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:37.868
Isn't that --

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.434
Here's another one.

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:42.734
For Miranda rights,
Trump said...

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:47.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.501
Also, when asked to define
"brief," Trump said...

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:52.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.033
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.434
Next up, the word "misdemeanor,"
Trump said...

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.267
"Miss Demeanor."

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:04.467
Up next, when asked to define
"sequester," Trump said...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.534 --> 00:04:13.367
And finally, for the word
"precedent," he said...

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:19.133
So, we'll see what happens.

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:21.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.834
Some news from overseas.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.033
Today, Chinese president
Xi Jinping travelled to Russia

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.100
to meet with
Vladimir Putin.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.801
Putin was just happy to get out
of his bunker,

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.367
while Xi was like,
"Worst spring break ever."

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:36.234
Yep, Putin and Xi were together
for over four hours,

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:38.400
waiting for the other one to sip
their drink first.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:49.067
[As Putin] "Let's trade. You
take mine, and I'll take yours.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.467
Let's trade again."

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:55.033
Switching gears, some business
news -- Taco bell just announced

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:57.467
that they are bringing back
two of their spiciest menu items

00:04:57.467 --> 00:05:00.667
ever, the Volcano Burrito
and Volcano Taco.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.100
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.701
I'm not sure about their slogan
for it though...

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.968
Wait, wait, wait.

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.467
What?

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.868
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.133
Some sports news.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.000
Well, guys. It was a crazy
weekend of March Madness.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.200
We're down to the sweet 16.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.534
Number 15, Princeton,
is the biggest underdog

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.200
left in the tournament.
Yeah.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.200
Marking --

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:27.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.267
Marking the first time
"underdog" and "Princeton"

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:31.033
have been
used in the same sentence.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.367
That's right, Princeton has
reached the sweet 16,

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.801
and they got --
they're super excited.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.234
I've got to say, celebrations at
Princeton are a bit different

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.501
than most teams.

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.234
For example, this was the scene
after Tennessee

00:05:41.234 --> 00:05:42.234
reached sweet 16.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:43.501
[ All cheering ]

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:45.567
-If you are playing
in the NCAA tournament,

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.834
this is the kind
of locker room you want.

00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:49.000
-[ Screeches ]
-Yep.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.934
And here's how Princeton
celebrated.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:53.434
[ Classical music plays ]
-Good game, chaps.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:55.467
-Hip, hip, hooray.

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:56.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.601 --> 00:05:59.234
-Different scene.

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.534
And finally, after the first
weekend of March Madness,

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:03.267
there are no more
perfect brackets.

00:06:03.267 --> 00:06:04.701
Yeah.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:08.033
Thanks to all the upsates -- the
upsets, everyone's bracket was

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.701
busted,
which isn't surprising.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.601
The chances of having
a perfect bracket are one

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.868
in nine quintillion.

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.667
In fact, the whole thing
inspired me to write

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:16.734
a tiny song.

00:06:16.734 --> 00:06:18.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:24.901
♪♪

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.901
We have a great show!

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:23.767
Florence Pugh is here tonight.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:26.367
Gaten Matarazzo is joining us.

00:07:26.367 --> 00:07:29.667
And we've got music from
Talib Kweli and Madlib.

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:32.534
Stick around. We'll be
right back with Florence Pugh.

00:07:32.534 --> 00:07:35.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:35.534 --> 00:07:38.968
